    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "description",
      "value": "[auto-routed: surprise=1.00] Execute a classical MD simulation on Ca-Si-Al-O glass to generate ion migration trajectories and compute temperature-dependent diffusivity, which will be used to test the non-Arrhenius hypothesis and extract activation energy parameters. This requires the md_pipeline skill with packing_tool and lammps_tool."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "skill",
      "value": "md_pipeline"
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "expected_prediction",
      "value": "The simulation will produce diffusivity values D(T) at multiple temperatures (e.g., 300K, 600K, 900K) showing non-Arrhenius behavior (curved Arrhenius plot), with apparent activation energy increasing at lower temperatures due to network connectivity effects."
    },
    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
